msgstr "Remove RAL from these IDEs:\n\n%s\nWhat the installer did is undone: the registry, the library path and the configuration go back to what they were, and the .bpl files it wrote are deleted. What was installed by hand leaves the registry and the configuration (the .bpl files stay on disk), with a record to undo it. Lazarus is rebuilt without the packages; the dependencies are not touched. Close the IDEs first.\n\nUninstall now?"

